r alphanumeric strings like '06AAECM4821F1ZX').\n   - NEVER create a line item for a Phone / Mobile / Contact Number.\n   - Every valid item MUST represent a product or service with a genuine unit quantity and unit price. If a row lacks a product description or represents invoice metadata, ignore it from items.\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:","Target":"import { sanitizeInvoiceData } from \"./privacyMasker.js\";\nimport { parseInvoiceText, isLikelyInvoice } from \"./invoiceTextParser.js\";\n\nconst GEMINI_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION = `\nYou are an invoice parsing engine for AUDIT IT.\n\nTASK:\n1. Examine the provided document or image.\n2. First, determine if this is a genuine business invoice, cash memo, purchase bill, or tax receipt.\n3. IF IT IS NOT an invoice (e.g. it is a person's photo, landscape, screenshot of a chat, unrelated document, or random text):\n   - Set is_valid_bill to false.\n   - Set rejection_reason explaining why (e.g. \"Uploaded image is not a financial bill or invoice\").\n   - Leave all financial fields null or empty.\n4. IF IT IS AN INVOICE:\n   - Set is_valid_bill to true.\n   - Extract the EXACT vendor name, GSTIN, invoice number, date, and line items (description, qty, rate, amount) visible on the bill.\n   - NEVER make up or hallucinate missing data or dummy items. If a field (like GSTIN or invoice number) is not present or unreadable, set it to null and append it to unreadable_fields.\n   - Extract exact declared amounts; DO NOT fix math mistakes in the extraction.\n\nReturn ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:"}}]}
